CS AUTO-NUDGE — SOURCE-AGE ALERT RESOLUTION LEDGER
Single-record template for Owen (shadow ledger). Use one row per alert event.

CASE CLASSIFICATION (select exactly one; do not reuse this row across classes)
  [ ] Source-age alert resolved before the recorded freshness limit (this template)
  [ ] Stale-state hold — decision(s) exceeded the limit, source still delayed → use stale-hold template
  [ ] Freshness-limit breach — decision(s) crossed the limit, incident-stop invoked → use breach template

IDENTIFIERS
  Alert ID:                    {{alert_id}}
  Ledger entry timestamp (UTC): {{entry_ts_utc}}
  Ledger window covered:        {{window_start}} → {{window_end}}
  Source under alert:           {{source_name}}           (qualifying-human-admin / external-system authority / active-CS-work / other)
  Source owner:                 {{source_owner}}
  Release authority for held state: Daniela (retained — this entry does not transfer it)
  Rollback authority:               Daniela (retained)

RELEASE-PREP CHECKLIST ITEMS SATISFIED (mark all five)
  [ ] Exercised each of the 5 governed fields across the 4 production consumers
  [ ] Verified the warning fired during the final 60 minutes before the recorded freshness limit
  [ ] Captured the affected consumer and the record count in the entry
  [ ] Notified Daniela and the named source owner
  [ ] Confirmed that crossing the actual limit still produces the existing visible field-specific hold
  Constraint: the warning cannot release, suppress, or decide a customer action.

FRESHNESS WINDOW
  Recorded freshness limit:    {{limit_ts_utc}}
  Alert fired at:              {{alert_fired_utc}}
  Alert-to-limit gap:          {{gap_minutes}} min        (must be ≤ 60 if the warning fired in the final hour)
  Resolved at:                 {{resolved_ts_utc}}
  Remaining freshness window at resolution:  {{remaining_minutes}} min     (e.g., 18)
  Did the limit cross before resolution?     {{yes / no}}                 (must be "no" for this template)

AFFECTED DECISIONS  (counted once in the primary denominator per the unique-decision rule)
  Affected consumer:                       {{consumer_name}}
  Record count:                            {{record_count}}
  Pending CS auto-nudge decisions at alert: {{pending_count}}
  Decisions recorded in audit history only (not double-counted): {{audit_only_count}}
  Governed-field disagreement observed:    {{none / list_fields}}
  No-status-difference check:               external-system authority / connector-auth / entitlement / qualifying-human-admin / CS-work — all unchanged.

FRESH REEVALUATION (post-refresh)
  Refresh action:                          {{refresh_action}}   (e.g., "Daniela restored qualifying-human-admin refresh")
  Fresh reevaluation completed at:         {{fresh_reeval_utc}}
  Outcome:
    Proceeded using current state:         {{proceeded_count}}
    Suppressed (active-CS-work / adoption in progress): {{suppressed_count}}
    Field-specific hold placed:            {{hold_count}}
    Customer correction required:          {{yes / no}}   (must be "no" for a clean alert-resolved entry)
    Decision manually released:            {{yes / no}}   (must be "no")
    Rollback invoked:                      {{yes / no}}   (must be "no")

FIELD-SPECIFIC HOLDS OBSERVED (complete only if any)
  Stale qualifying-human-admin:            {{count}}
  Unresolved external-system authority:    {{count}}
  Active-CS-work suppression:              {{count}}
  Other (specify):                         {{count}} — {{reason}}

INCIDENT STOP
  Incident-stop invoked:                   {{yes / no}}   (must be "no" for alert-resolved)
  If yes, incident ID and stop timestamp:  {{incident_id}} / {{stop_ts_utc}}
  If no, confirm adjacent controls held:   {{confirmed}}

ROLLBACK
  Rollback observation:                    {{none / description}}
  Coordinated rollback available but unused: {{confirmed}}
  Adjacent-message eligibility assertion:  {{none present / suppressed}} — Ines lane; no adjacent message assumes eligibility for the affected decisions.

LEDGER INTEGRITY RULES (each must hold for this entry)
  [ ] Each scheduled decision appears once in the primary denominator.
  [ ] Holds and fresh-check outcomes are retained in audit history, not double-counted.
  [ ] The alert itself is not counted as an additional hold or decision (unique-decision + warning-history rule).
  [ ] No status difference across the five governed dimensions.
  [ ] No customer correction in this entry.
  [ ] No rollback in this entry.
  [ ] Daniela retains release and rollback control; this resolution does not transfer either.

EVIDENCE CLASSIFICATION
  Entry is:    {{interim operational monitoring / Q3 evidence-lock / board-facing / first-live operating-review prep}}
  Feeds review: {{review_date}}   (e.g., the June 13 first-live operating review)
  Legacy-path decision status:          {{open / closed}} — independent of this entry
  Operational-freshness evidence only?   {{yes / no — reason}}
  Measurement-only caveat (per July 31 Q3 evidence-lock rule): this template does not assume the source-age alert is live or effective; entries are operational monitoring until that assumption is upgraded.

SIGN-OFF
  Prepared by: Owen
  Reviewed by: {{reviewer}}
  Date:        {{date_utc}}

Notes on use:
- One alert → one row. Do not split a single alert across rows or merge multiple alerts into one.
- If any "must be no" field flips to yes, stop: this is no longer an alert-resolved event and the stale-hold or breach template applies.
- Keep the five governed fields, four production consumers, three field-specific hold reasons, and the warning-cannot-act constraint verbatim — they are the taxonomy other evidence already cites.
